  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **Fixes**:\n  - `GameUpdateValueConverter` now reads a single JSON object for a game update `value`. TheGamesDB returns one for some edit types, and the converter previously threw — which aborted the whole paginated `Games/Updates` walk. Because the caller's last-edit cursor only advances on a completed walk, every subsequent run replayed the same pages and failed on the same record, so an import could never get past it.\n  - `GameUpdateValueConverter` also accepts boolean values.\n  - The exception for a genuinely unreadable value now names the token type and byte offset instead of the bare \"Unexpected JSON token type.\", which carried no way to identify the offending record.",
